      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHOOBEES BOMB (3) gets top billing on profile rather than last-start performance, as she was beaten just under four metres as a very short odds-on favourite at Wagin. The counter is her Narrogin record and proven distance form, which give her the strongest winning platform if she returns to her best. ZILLIONAIRE (2) draws well and is the main threat after a Collie third beaten just over two metres and a sound Gloucester Park fourth, although the maiden record remains the query. ROCKSTAR WORLD (7) has claims off his Northam third two back and was not disgraced here last start, but the second row means he needs a suitable trail. STRANIERO DEL MARE (5) was plain at Gloucester Park, yet her Pinjarra third in a sharper 1:57.9 mile rate gives her enough substance to run into the minor money if she repeats it.",
